1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:05,837
In this lesson, you'll learn to reply on
any channel from one place: text, email,

2
00:00:05,837 --> 00:00:08,736
WhatsApp, Facebook,
Instagram and live chat.

3
00:00:08,736 --> 00:00:12,690
One thread per customer, and
no more switching between apps.

4
00:00:13,551 --> 00:00:14,409
Here's Olivia.

5
00:00:14,409 --> 00:00:17,659
She first messaged us on
Facebook after seeing an ad.

6
00:00:17,659 --> 00:00:21,093
We followed up by email, and
this morning she's texting.

7
00:00:21,093 --> 00:00:26,121
It's all one thread, in order, so anyone
on your team can pick it up with the full

8
00:00:26,121 --> 00:00:26,489
story.

9
00:00:27,341 --> 00:00:31,407
Under every message, you can see
which channel it came through.

10
00:00:31,407 --> 00:00:36,634
Messages with the purple AI label were
written by your AI agent, not by a person.

11
00:00:36,634 --> 00:00:38,699
You'll set that up in Module 10.

12
00:00:39,548 --> 00:00:42,237
To reply, use the composer at the bottom.

13
00:00:42,237 --> 00:00:44,860
The row of tabs is the channel switcher.

14
00:00:44,860 --> 00:00:49,254
Kyntlo picks the channel the customer
used last, which is SMS here.

15
00:00:49,254 --> 00:00:54,238
The From and To line shows exactly which
number you're sending from, and to.

16
00:00:55,090 --> 00:00:58,572
Olivia asked about Thursday,
so let's text her back.

17
00:00:58,572 --> 00:01:03,258
Type your reply, keep an eye on the
character counter, and click Send.

18
00:01:03,258 --> 00:01:05,601
One text segment is 160 characters.

19
00:01:05,601 --> 00:01:09,819
When Olivia answers, her reply
lands right back in this thread.

20
00:01:10,670 --> 00:01:11,663
Prefer WhatsApp?

21
00:01:11,663 --> 00:01:16,691
Click the WhatsApp tab, and the same box
now sends through your WhatsApp Business

22
00:01:16,691 --> 00:01:17,126
number.

23
00:01:17,126 --> 00:01:21,967
A quick note on plans: texting and
WhatsApp are included from the Growth plan,

24
00:01:21,967 --> 00:01:24,264
and WhatsApp itself is a paid add-on.

25
00:01:24,264 --> 00:01:29,043
One WhatsApp rule to know: if the customer
hasn't messaged you in the last 24

26
00:01:29,043 --> 00:01:32,209
hours, you start with an
approved template message.

27
00:01:33,061 --> 00:01:35,373
For something longer, switch to Email.

28
00:01:35,373 --> 00:01:39,693
You get a subject line, and the reply
comes from your business address.

29
00:01:39,693 --> 00:01:42,309
Use email for treatment
plans, attachments,

30
00:01:42,309 --> 00:01:44,986
and anything the customer
will want to keep.

31
00:01:47,636 --> 00:01:51,499
Facebook and Instagram messages
work exactly the same way.

32
00:01:51,499 --> 00:01:56,628
Ava messaged our Instagram account, so
the Instagram tab is already selected.

33
00:01:56,628 --> 00:02:00,092
Your reply goes back as an
Instagram direct message,

34
00:02:00,092 --> 00:02:02,424
and she never has to leave the app.

35
00:02:03,277 --> 00:02:05,125
Website chat is no different.

36
00:02:05,125 --> 00:02:09,077
Mason asked a question through
the chat widget on our website,

37
00:02:09,077 --> 00:02:14,239
so the Live Chat tab is selected, and he
sees your answer right there in the chat

38
00:02:14,239 --> 00:02:14,685
window.

39
00:02:14,685 --> 00:02:17,872
Live chat works on every
plan, so even on Starter,

40
00:02:17,872 --> 00:02:20,166
website visitors can reach you here.

41
00:02:21,018 --> 00:02:23,034
One more tab: Internal Comment.

42
00:02:23,034 --> 00:02:25,311
It's a note only your team can see.

43
00:02:25,311 --> 00:02:29,929
Use it to hand over context, like
"Mason prefers evening appointments",

44
00:02:29,929 --> 00:02:32,271
without the customer ever seeing it.

45
00:02:33,123 --> 00:02:34,258
Here's a pro tip.

46
00:02:34,258 --> 00:02:36,930
Reply on the channel the customer chose.

47
00:02:36,930 --> 00:02:41,205
If someone messages you on
Instagram, answer on Instagram first.

48
00:02:41,205 --> 00:02:43,810
Jumping to a phone call can feel pushy.

49
00:02:43,810 --> 00:02:47,416
Once they're comfortable,
ask for their mobile number,

50
00:02:47,416 --> 00:02:49,554
so you can text reminders later.

51
00:02:50,407 --> 00:02:51,093
Great work!

52
00:02:51,093 --> 00:02:55,397
Next, you'll learn to reply even
faster, with snippets and templates,

53
00:02:55,397 --> 00:02:57,580
and to schedule messages for later.

54
00:02:57,580 --> 00:02:58,453
See you there.
